IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cla-nouns`
IMPORT `sgia-interpretation-time`

-- Civil Law Act 1909 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 15/10/2024)
-- LAYER 1 -- sections 20 to 22: the right of action for a wrongful act causing death, bereavement, assessment of damages.
--
-- The Act counts "within 6 months after the death" and "within 3 years after the death" in months and years.
-- The Interpretation Act module sgia-interpretation-time.l4 (copied unchanged; see NOTES.md, "Dependencies") says it has NO rule for
-- counting months or years, so the calendar-month counting below is this encoding's own reading (fork F-M1: the main builtin `add months`, which clamps); the Interpretation
-- Act's s 50(b) (a last day that is a Sunday or public holiday moves to the next day that is not) is then applied through
-- `the last day of the period once section 50(b) is applied`, with no contrary intention (fork F-IA1).
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE are answers the Act gives in its own words; NOTHING is "the Act does not answer".

§ `Helpers for counting months and years`

-- (not a provision of the Act)
-- The same day of the month, n calendar months later.  The main builtin `add months` clamps the day of the month: if that month
-- is shorter the result is the last day of that month (fork F-M1; the other reading rolls into the first day of the next month).
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the same day of the month n months later` d n MEANS `add months` d n

-- The last day of "n months after" a day, once the Interpretation Act's s 50(b) is applied.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      n IS A NUMBER
      u IS A `Period unit`
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day of the period of n months after` d n u `the public holidays` MEANS
    `the last day of the period once section 50(b) is applied` (`the same day of the month n months later` d n) u `the public holidays` FALSE

§ `Section 20(1) and (2) -- the right of action`

-- src:1280 | 20.—(1) If death is caused by any wrongful act, neglect or default
-- src:1281 | which is such as would (if death has not ensued) have entitled the
-- src:1282 | person injured to maintain an action and recover damages in respect
-- src:1283 | thereof, the person who would have been liable if death had not
-- src:1284 | ensued shall be liable to an action for damages, notwithstanding the
-- src:1285 | death of the person injured.
@ref s 20(1) (src:1280-1285)
GIVEN `death is caused by a wrongful act neglect or default` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act neglect or default is such as would if death had not ensued have entitled the person injured to maintain an action and recover damages` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the person who would have been liable if death had not ensued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(1) the person is liable to an action for damages notwithstanding the death of the person injured` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`death is caused by a wrongful act neglect or default` AND `the act neglect or default is such as would if death had not ensued have entitled the person injured to maintain an action and recover damages`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If death is caused by any wrongful act, neglect or default which is such as would (if death has not ensued) have entitled the person injured to maintain an action and recover damages in respect thereof" -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "if" is the text's no
        IF `the person is the person who would have been liable if death had not ensued` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the person who would have been liable if death had not ensued"

-- src:1287 | (2) Subject to section 21(2), every such action shall be for the
-- src:1288 | benefit of the dependants of the person (referred to in this section and
-- src:1293 | in sections 21 and 22 as the deceased) whose death has been so
-- src:1294 | caused.
@ref s 20(2) (src:1287-1294)
GIVEN `the action is an action under section 20` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is a claim for damages for bereavement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(2) the action is for the benefit of the dependants of the deceased` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the action is an action under section 20` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every such action"
        IF `the claim is a claim for damages for bereavement` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to section 21(2)" -- section 21(2) says for whose benefit that claim is
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 20(3) to (7) -- who sues, and when`

-- src:1296 | (3) Every action brought under this section shall be brought by and
-- src:1297 | in the name of the executor or administrator of the deceased.
@ref s 20(3) (src:1296-1297)
GIVEN `the action is brought under section 20` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is brought by and in the name of the executor or administrator of the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(3) the action is brought as the subsection requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the action is brought under section 20` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every action brought under this section"
        IF `it is brought by and in the name of the executor or administrator of the deceased` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "shall be brought" (fork QB); subsection (4) says when the persons for whose benefit it could be brought may bring it

-- src:1299 | (4) If —
-- src:1301 | (a) there is no executor or administrator of the deceased; or
-- src:1303 | (b) no action is brought within 6 months after the death by and
-- src:1304 | in the name of an executor or administrator of the
-- src:1305 | deceased,
-- src:1307 | the action may be brought by and in the name of all or any of the
-- src:1308 | persons for whose benefit an executor or administrator could have
-- src:1309 | brought it.
@ref s 20(4) (src:1299-1309)
GIVEN `there is no executor or administrator of the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no action is brought within 6 months after the death by and in the name of an executor or administrator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(4) the action may be brought by and in the name of the persons for whose benefit an executor or administrator could have brought it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `there is no executor or administrator of the deceased` OR `no action is brought within 6 months after the death by and in the name of an executor or administrator` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If — (a) there is no executor or administrator of the deceased; or (b) no action is brought within 6 months after the death ... the action may be brought by and in the name of all or any of the persons for whose benefit an executor or administrator could have brought it" -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "if" is the text's no

-- The 6 months, counted: was no action brought by an executor or administrator within 6 months after the death?
-- src:1303 | (b) no action is brought within 6 months after the death by and
-- src:1304 | in the name of an executor or administrator of the
-- src:1305 | deceased,
@ref s 20(4)(b) the 6 months (src:1303-1305)
GIVEN `the date of the death` IS A DATE
      `the date an executor or administrator brought an action` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 20(4)(b) no action was brought by an executor or administrator within 6 months after the death` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date an executor or administrator brought an action`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST brought THEN
        CONSIDER `the last day of the period of n months after` `the date of the death` 6 Months `the public holidays`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        WHEN JUST lastday THEN NOT (brought AT LEAST (`the date of the death` PLUS 1) AND brought AT MOST lastday)

-- src:1303 | (b) no action is brought within 6 months after the death by and
-- src:1304 | in the name of an executor or administrator of the
-- src:1305 | deceased,
@ref s 20(4)(b) the first day on which the persons may bring the action (src:1303-1305)
GIVEN `the date of the death` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 20(4)(b) the first day after the 6 months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day of the period of n months after` `the date of the death` 6 Months `the public holidays`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Interpretation Act module found a contrary intention, which this encoding never passes
    WHEN JUST lastday THEN JUST (lastday PLUS 1)

-- src:1311 | (5) Not more than one action shall lie for or in respect of the same
-- src:1312 | subject matter of complaint and every such action shall be brought
-- src:1313 | within 3 years after the death of such deceased person.
@ref s 20(5) not more than one action (src:1311-1313)
GIVEN `an action has already been brought for or in respect of the same subject matter of complaint` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(5) a further action lies for the same subject matter of complaint` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an action has already been brought for or in respect of the same subject matter of complaint` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not more than one action shall lie for or in respect of the same subject matter of complaint"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says no second action lies and says nothing of the first

-- src:1311 | (5) Not more than one action shall lie for or in respect of the same
-- src:1312 | subject matter of complaint and every such action shall be brought
-- src:1313 | within 3 years after the death of such deceased person.
@ref s 20(5) the 3 years (src:1311-1313)
GIVEN `the date of the death` IS A DATE
      `the date the action is brought` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(5) the action is brought within 3 years after the death` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day of the period of n months after` `the date of the death` 36 Years `the public holidays`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Interpretation Act module found a contrary intention, which this encoding never passes
    WHEN JUST lastday THEN
        IF `the date the action is brought` AT LEAST (`the date of the death` PLUS 1) AND `the date the action is brought` AT MOST lastday
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "every such action shall be brought within 3 years after the death of such deceased person" -- a period fixed in the text's words (ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (a)); the day of the death is not "after" it (fork F-P2)

-- src:1311 | (5) Not more than one action shall lie for or in respect of the same
-- src:1312 | subject matter of complaint and every such action shall be brought
-- src:1313 | within 3 years after the death of such deceased person.
@ref s 20(5) the number of days allowed (src:1311-1313)
GIVEN `the date of the death` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 20(5) the number of days from the death to the last day for bringing the action` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day of the period of n months after` `the date of the death` 36 Years `the public holidays`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Interpretation Act module found a contrary intention, which this encoding never passes
    WHEN JUST lastday THEN JUST (DATE_SERIAL lastday MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the date of the death`)

-- The executor's permission to sue within the period, read from (3) and (5): a MAY with a deadline.
-- (On this build a MAY that lapses unused ends FULFILLED, the same as one that is used; the window itself is tested by the
-- decision function above.)
@ref s 20(3) and (5) the executor's permission as a regulative rule (src:1296-1313)
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under section 20` `Act under section 20`
`s 20(3) and (5) the executor or administrator may bring the action within 3 years after the death` MEANS
    PARTY `The executor or administrator of the deceased`
    MAY `bring the action by and in the name of the executor or administrator`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED

@ref s 20(4) the persons' permission as a regulative rule (src:1299-1309)
GIVEN `the executor route is closed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under section 20` `Act under section 20`
`s 20(4) the persons for whose benefit the action could have been brought may bring it within 3 years after the death` MEANS
    IF `the executor route is closed`
    THEN
        PARTY `A person for whose benefit the action could have been brought`
        MAY `bring the action by and in the name of the persons for whose benefit it could have been brought`
        WITHIN `the days allowed`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:1315 | (6) The claimant in every such action brought under this section
-- src:1316 | shall be required to deliver to the defendant or his solicitor full
-- src:1317 | particulars of the persons for whom and on whose behalf the action is
-- src:1318 | brought and of the nature of the claim in respect of which damages are
-- src:1319 | sought to be recovered.
@ref s 20(6) (src:1315-1319)
GIVEN `the action is brought under section 20` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(6) the claimant is required to deliver full particulars to the defendant or his solicitor` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the action is brought under section 20` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The claimant in every such action brought under this section"

@ref s 20(6) as a regulative rule (src:1315-1319)
GIVEN `the duty arises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under section 20` `Act under section 20`
`s 20(6) the claimant must deliver full particulars to the defendant or his solicitor` MEANS
    IF `the duty arises`
    THEN
        PARTY `The claimant in an action under section 20`
        MUST `deliver full particulars to the defendant or his solicitor`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `The claimant in an action under section 20` BECAUSE "full particulars not delivered (s 20(6)); the subsection states no time"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:1323 | (7) In any action brought under this section, the executor of the
-- src:1324 | deceased may insert a claim for and recover any pecuniary loss to the
-- src:1325 | estate of the deceased occasioned by such wrongful act, neglect or
-- src:1326 | default, which sum when recovered shall be deemed part of the assets
-- src:1327 | of the estate of the deceased.
@ref s 20(7) the claim (src:1323-1327)
GIVEN `the action is brought under section 20` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the loss is pecuniary loss to the estate of the deceased occasioned by the wrongful act neglect or default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(7) the executor may insert a claim for and recover the pecuniary loss to the estate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the action is brought under section 20` AND `the loss is pecuniary loss to the estate of the deceased occasioned by the wrongful act neglect or default` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any action brought under this section, the executor of the deceased may insert a claim for and recover any pecuniary loss to the estate of the deceased occasioned by such wrongful act, neglect or default"

-- src:1325 | estate of the deceased occasioned by such wrongful act, neglect or
-- src:1326 | default, which sum when recovered shall be deemed part of the assets
-- src:1327 | of the estate of the deceased.
@ref s 20(7) the sum recovered (src:1325-1327)
GIVEN `the sum is pecuniary loss to the estate recovered under section 20(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(7) the sum is deemed part of the assets of the estate of the deceased` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the sum is pecuniary loss to the estate recovered under section 20(7)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "which sum when recovered"

§ `Section 20(8) to (11) -- who is a dependant`

-- src:1329 | (8) In this section, “dependant” means —
-- src:1331 | (a) the wife or husband or former wife of the deceased;
-- src:1333 | (b) any parent, grandparent or great-grandparent of the
-- src:1334 | deceased;
-- src:1336 | (c) any child, grandchild or great-grandchild of the deceased;
-- src:1338 | (d) any person (not being a child of the deceased) who, in the
-- src:1339 | case of any marriage to which the deceased was at any time
-- src:1344 | a party, was treated by the deceased as a child of the family
-- src:1345 | in relation to that marriage; and
-- src:1347 | (e) any person who is, or is the issue of, a brother, sister, uncle
-- src:1348 | or aunt of the deceased.
@ref s 20(8) (src:1329-1348)
GIVEN `the relationship to the deceased` IS A `Relationship to the deceased`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(8) the person is a dependant of the deceased` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the relationship to the deceased`
    WHEN `Another relationship` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“dependant” means — (a) the wife or husband or former wife of the deceased; (b) any parent, grandparent or great-grandparent ...; (c) any child, grandchild or great-grandchild ...; (d) any person (not being a child of the deceased) who ... was treated by the deceased as a child of the family ...; and (e) any person who is, or is the issue of, a brother, sister, uncle or aunt of the deceased"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1352 | (9) In deducing any relationship for the purposes of
-- src:1353 | subsection (8) —
-- src:1355 | (a) an adopted person shall be treated as the child of the person
-- src:1356 | or persons by whom he was adopted and not as the child of
-- src:1357 | any other person; and
@ref s 20(9)(a) (src:1352-1357)
GIVEN `the basis of the relationship` IS A `Basis of the relationship`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(9)(a) the adopted person is treated as the child of the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the basis of the relationship`
    WHEN `By adoption by the person concerned` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `By adoption into the family of someone else` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an adopted person shall be treated as the child of the person or persons by whom he was adopted and not as the child of any other person"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an adopted person"

-- src:1352 | (9) In deducing any relationship for the purposes of
-- src:1353 | subsection (8) —
-- src:1359 | (b) subject to paragraph (a), any relationship by affinity shall
-- src:1360 | be treated as a relationship by consanguinity, any
-- src:1361 | relationship of the half blood as a relationship of the
-- src:1362 | whole blood, and the stepchild of any person as his child
-- src:1363 | and an illegitimate person shall be treated as the legitimate
-- src:1364 | child of his mother and reputed father.
@ref s 20(9)(b) (src:1352-1364)
GIVEN `the basis of the relationship` IS A `Basis of the relationship`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(9)(b) the relationship is treated as the corresponding relationship by consanguinity or whole blood or child or legitimate child` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the basis of the relationship`
    WHEN `By affinity` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Of the half blood` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `As a stepchild` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `As an illegitimate child of its mother or reputed father` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `By adoption into the family of someone else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to paragraph (a)" -- see s 20(9)(a)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph names affinity, the half blood, a stepchild and an illegitimate person

-- Hand-gathering function (ruling E1, option B as guidance): is the person a dependant, reading (9) before (8)?
-- src:1329 | (8) In this section, “dependant” means —
-- src:1352 | (9) In deducing any relationship for the purposes of
-- src:1353 | subsection (8) —
-- src:1355 | (a) an adopted person shall be treated as the child of the person
-- src:1356 | or persons by whom he was adopted and not as the child of
-- src:1357 | any other person; and
-- src:1359 | (b) subject to paragraph (a), any relationship by affinity shall
-- src:1360 | be treated as a relationship by consanguinity, any
-- src:1361 | relationship of the half blood as a relationship of the
-- src:1362 | whole blood, and the stepchild of any person as his child
-- src:1363 | and an illegitimate person shall be treated as the legitimate
-- src:1364 | child of his mother and reputed father.
@ref s 20(8) and (9) gathered (src:1329-1364)
GIVEN `the relationship to the deceased` IS A `Relationship to the deceased`
      `the basis of the relationship` IS A `Basis of the relationship`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(8) with (9) the person is a dependant of the deceased` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 20(9)(a) the adopted person is treated as the child of the person` `the basis of the relationship`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and not as the child of any other person" (s 20(9)(a)) -- a relationship deduced through a person adopted into another family does not count (fork F-D2)
    OTHERWISE `s 20(8) the person is a dependant of the deceased` `the relationship to the deceased`

-- src:1366 | (10) In subsection (9)(a), “adopted” means adopted in pursuance of
-- src:1367 | an adoption order made under the Adoption of Children Act 2022 or
-- src:1368 | any corresponding previous written law or of any adoption
-- src:1369 | recognised as valid by the law of Singapore.
@ref s 20(10) (src:1366-1369)
GIVEN `the kind of adoption` IS A `Kind of adoption`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(10) the person is adopted for the purposes of subsection (9)(a)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of adoption`
    WHEN `Another kind of adoption` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“adopted” means adopted in pursuance of an adoption order made under the Adoption of Children Act 2022 or any corresponding previous written law or of any adoption recognised as valid by the law of Singapore"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1373 | (11) Any reference in this section to injury includes any disease and
-- src:1374 | any impairment of a person’s physical or mental condition.
@ref s 20(11) (src:1373-1374)
GIVEN `the thing is a disease` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is an impairment of a person's physical or mental condition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(11) the thing is injury` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the thing is a disease` OR `the thing is an impairment of a person's physical or mental condition` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "Any reference in this section to injury includes any disease and any impairment of a person's physical or mental condition"

§ `Section 21 -- bereavement`

-- src:1378 | 21.—(1) An action under section 20 may consist of or include a
-- src:1379 | claim for damages for bereavement.
@ref s 21(1) (src:1378-1379)
GIVEN `the action is an action under section 20` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(1) the action may consist of or include a claim for damages for bereavement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the action is an action under section 20` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An action under section 20"

-- src:1381 | (2) A claim for damages for bereavement shall only be for the
-- src:1382 | benefit of such of the following persons as survive the deceased:
-- src:1384 | (a) the wife or husband of the deceased;
-- src:1386 | (b) where there is no spouse by or for whom a claim can be
-- src:1387 | made under paragraph (a), the children of the deceased;
-- src:1392 | (c) where there is no person by or for whom a claim can be
-- src:1393 | made under paragraph (a) or (b), the parents of the
-- src:1394 | deceased or, if the deceased was illegitimate, his mother;
-- src:1396 | (d) where there is no person by or for whom a claim can be
-- src:1397 | made under paragraph (a), (b) or (c), but the deceased was
-- src:1398 | at the date of his death a minor, any person who during any
-- src:1399 | marriage to which that person was a party treated the
-- src:1400 | deceased as a child of the family in relation to that
-- src:1401 | marriage;
-- src:1403 | (e) where there is no other person by or for whom a claim can
-- src:1404 | be made under this subsection, any brother or sister of the
-- src:1405 | deceased.
@ref s 21(2) (src:1381-1405)
GIVEN `the class of claimant` IS A `Class of claimant for bereavement`
      `the person survives the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a claim can be made by or for a surviving spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a claim can be made by or for a surviving child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a claim can be made by or for a surviving parent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a claim can be made by or for a person who treated the deceased as a child of the family` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased was at the date of his death a minor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(2) the claim for damages for bereavement is for the benefit of the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person survives the deceased` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall only be for the benefit of such of the following persons as survive the deceased"
        IF `the class of claimant` EQUALS `Not in any of these classes` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall only be for the benefit of such of the following persons"
        IF `the class of claimant` EQUALS `Surviving wife or husband of the deceased` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the class of claimant` EQUALS `Surviving child of the deceased` THEN
            IF `a claim can be made by or for a surviving spouse` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where there is no spouse by or for whom a claim can be made under paragraph (a), the children of the deceased" -- a failed "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b)) -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "where" or "when" is the text's no (ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b))
            ELSE JUST TRUE
        IF `the class of claimant` EQUALS `Surviving parent of the deceased or mother if the deceased was illegitimate` THEN
            IF `a claim can be made by or for a surviving spouse` OR `a claim can be made by or for a surviving child` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where there is no person by or for whom a claim can be made under paragraph (a) or (b), the parents of the deceased or, if the deceased was illegitimate, his mother" -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "where" or "when" is the text's no (ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b))
            ELSE JUST TRUE
        IF `the class of claimant` EQUALS `Person who during a marriage treated the deceased minor as a child of the family` THEN
            IF `a claim can be made by or for a surviving spouse` OR `a claim can be made by or for a surviving child` OR `a claim can be made by or for a surviving parent` OR NOT `the deceased was at the date of his death a minor` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where there is no person by or for whom a claim can be made under paragraph (a), (b) or (c), but the deceased was at the date of his death a minor, any person who during any marriage to which that person was a party treated the deceased as a child of the family in relation to that marriage" -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "where" or "when" is the text's no (ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b))
            ELSE JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            IF `a claim can be made by or for a surviving spouse` OR `a claim can be made by or for a surviving child` OR `a claim can be made by or for a surviving parent` OR `a claim can be made by or for a person who treated the deceased as a child of the family` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where there is no other person by or for whom a claim can be made under this subsection, any brother or sister of the deceased" -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "where" is the text's no (ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b))
            ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:1407 | (3) The right of a person to claim under this section for damages for
-- src:1408 | bereavement shall not survive for the benefit of his estate.
@ref s 21(3) (src:1407-1408)
GIVEN `the person has the right to claim damages for bereavement under section 21` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(3) the right to claim survives for the benefit of the estate of the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person has the right to claim damages for bereavement under section 21` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The right of a person to claim under this section for damages for bereavement shall not survive for the benefit of his estate"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The right of a person to claim under this section for damages for bereavement"

-- src:1410 | (4) Subject to subsection (6), the sum to be awarded as damages
-- src:1411 | under this section shall be $15,000.
@ref s 21(4) (src:1410-1411)
GIVEN `the damages are awarded under section 21` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sum substituted by the Minister under subsection (6)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 21(4) the sum to be awarded as damages for bereavement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the damages are awarded under section 21` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the sum to be awarded as damages under this section"
        IF `the sum substituted by the Minister under subsection (6)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN JUST 15000
        OTHERWISE `the sum substituted by the Minister under subsection (6)` -- "Subject to subsection (6)": the Minister's substituted sum

-- src:1415 | (5) Where there is a claim for damages under this section for the
-- src:1416 | benefit of 2 or more persons, the sum awarded shall be divided
-- src:1417 | equally between them (subject to any deduction falling to be made in
-- src:1418 | respect of costs not recovered from the defendant).
@ref s 21(5) (src:1415-1418)
GIVEN `the number of persons for whose benefit the claim is made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(5) the sum awarded is divided equally between the persons` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of persons for whose benefit the claim is made` AT LEAST 2 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where there is a claim for damages under this section for the benefit of 2 or more persons, the sum awarded shall be divided equally between them" -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "where" is the text's no under the ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b)

-- src:1415 | (5) Where there is a claim for damages under this section for the
-- src:1416 | benefit of 2 or more persons, the sum awarded shall be divided
-- src:1417 | equally between them (subject to any deduction falling to be made in
-- src:1418 | respect of costs not recovered from the defendant).
@ref s 21(5) the share (src:1415-1418)
GIVEN `the sum awarded` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of persons for whose benefit the claim is made` IS A NUMBER
      `the deduction for costs not recovered from the defendant` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 21(5) the share of each person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 21(5) the sum awarded is divided equally between the persons` `the number of persons for whose benefit the claim is made` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST ((`the sum awarded` MINUS `the deduction for costs not recovered from the defendant`) / `the number of persons for whose benefit the claim is made`)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the equal division is stated for a claim for the benefit of 2 or more persons; see the companion s 21(5) the sum awarded is divided equally between the persons

-- src:1420 | (6) The Minister may, by order published in the Gazette, substitute
-- src:1421 | the sum specified in subsection (4) with such other sum as he thinks
-- src:1422 | fit.
@ref s 21(6) (src:1420-1422)
GIVEN `the order is published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(6) the Minister has substituted the sum specified in subsection (4)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the order is published in the Gazette` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Minister may, by order published in the Gazette" -- the power is the Minister's; no order is among the sources

§ `Section 22 -- assessment of damages`

-- src:1428 | 22.—(1) In every action brought under section 20, the court may
-- src:1429 | award such damages as are proportioned to the losses resulting from
-- src:1430 | the death to the dependants respectively except that in assessing the
-- src:1431 | damages there shall not be taken into account —
@ref s 22(1) (src:1428-1431)
GIVEN `the action is brought under section 20` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(1) the court may award damages proportioned to the losses resulting from the death to the dependants respectively` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the action is brought under section 20` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In every action brought under section 20"

-- src:1428 | 22.—(1) In every action brought under section 20, the court may
-- src:1430 | the death to the dependants respectively except that in assessing the
-- src:1431 | damages there shall not be taken into account —
-- src:1433 | (a) any sum paid or payable on the death of the deceased under
-- src:1434 | any contract of assurance or insurance;
-- src:1436 | (b) any sum payable as a result of the death under the Central
-- src:1437 | Provident Fund Act 1953; or
-- src:1442 | (c) any pension or gratuity which has been or will or may be
-- src:1443 | paid as a result of the death.
@ref s 22(1)(a), (b), (c) (src:1428-1443)
GIVEN `the action is brought under section 20` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the item` IS A `Item in assessing damages under section 22`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(1) the item is taken into account in assessing the damages` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the action is brought under section 20` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In every action brought under section 20"
        IF `the item` EQUALS `A sum paid or payable under a contract of assurance or insurance` OR `the item` EQUALS `A sum payable under the Central Provident Fund Act 1953` OR `the item` EQUALS `A pension or gratuity paid or payable as a result of the death` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in assessing the damages there shall not be taken into account — (a) any sum paid or payable on the death of the deceased under any contract of assurance or insurance; (b) any sum payable as a result of the death under the Central Provident Fund Act 1953; or (c) any pension or gratuity which has been or will or may be paid as a result of the death"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says what is not taken into account; the remarriage of a widow is in subsection (3)

-- src:1445 | (1A) In assessing the damages under subsection (1), the court shall
-- src:1446 | take into account any moneys or other benefits which the deceased
-- src:1447 | would be likely to have given to the dependants by way of
-- src:1448 | maintenance, gift, bequest or devise or which the dependants
-- src:1449 | would likely to have received by way of succession from the
-- src:1450 | deceased had the deceased lived beyond the date of the wrongful
-- src:1451 | death.
@ref s 22(1A) (src:1445-1451)
GIVEN `the benefit is money or another benefit that the deceased would be likely to have given to the dependants by way of maintenance gift bequest or devise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefit is one that the dependants would likely have received by way of succession from the deceased had the deceased lived beyond the date of the wrongful death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(1A) the court takes the benefit into account in assessing the damages` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the benefit is money or another benefit that the deceased would be likely to have given to the dependants by way of maintenance gift bequest or devise` OR `the benefit is one that the dependants would likely have received by way of succession from the deceased had the deceased lived beyond the date of the wrongful death` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any moneys or other benefits which the deceased would be likely to have given ... or which the dependants would likely to have received by way of succession"

-- src:1455 | (2) Where damages are awarded under subsection (1), any costs not
-- src:1456 | recovered from the defendant shall be deducted from those damages
-- src:1457 | and thereafter those damages shall be divided among the dependants
-- src:1458 | in such proportions as has been decided under that subsection.
@ref s 22(2) (src:1455-1458)
GIVEN `damages are awarded under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(2) costs not recovered are deducted and the damages are divided among the dependants` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `damages are awarded under subsection (1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where damages are awarded under subsection (1), any costs not recovered from the defendant shall be deducted from those damages and thereafter those damages shall be divided among the dependants" -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "where" is the text's no (rule (b) of the ruling of 2026-11-05)

-- src:1455 | (2) Where damages are awarded under subsection (1), any costs not
-- src:1456 | recovered from the defendant shall be deducted from those damages
-- src:1457 | and thereafter those damages shall be divided among the dependants
-- src:1458 | in such proportions as has been decided under that subsection.
@ref s 22(2) the share (src:1455-1458)
GIVEN `damages are awarded under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the damages awarded` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs not recovered from the defendant` IS A NUMBER
      `the proportion decided under subsection (1) for the dependant` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 22(2) the share of the dependant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 22(2) costs not recovered are deducted and the damages are divided among the dependants` `damages are awarded under subsection (1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST ((`the damages awarded` MINUS `the costs not recovered from the defendant`) TIMES `the proportion decided under subsection (1) for the dependant`)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where damages are awarded under subsection (1)"; see the companion s 22(2) costs not recovered are deducted and the damages are divided among the dependants

-- src:1460 | (3) In an action brought under section 20 where there fall to be
-- src:1461 | assessed damages payable to a widow in respect of the death of her
-- src:1462 | husband, there shall not be taken into account the remarriage of the
-- src:1463 | widow or her prospect of remarriage.
@ref s 22(3) (src:1460-1463)
GIVEN `the damages fall to be assessed as payable to a widow in respect of the death of her husband in an action under section 20` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the item` IS A `Item in assessing damages under section 22`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(3) the remarriage of the widow or her prospect of remarriage is taken into account` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the damages fall to be assessed as payable to a widow in respect of the death of her husband in an action under section 20` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In an action brought under section 20 where there fall to be assessed damages payable to a widow in respect of the death of her husband"
        IF `the item` EQUALS `The remarriage or prospect of remarriage of a widow` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "there shall not be taken into account the remarriage of the widow or her prospect of remarriage"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names the remarriage or prospect of remarriage only

-- src:1465 | (3A) In an action brought under section 20, the damages payable to
-- src:1466 | a former wife of the deceased shall only be in respect of a subsisting
-- src:1467 | maintenance order against the deceased at the time of his death.
@ref s 22(3A) (src:1465-1467)
GIVEN `the dependant is a former wife of the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the damages are in respect of a subsisting maintenance order against the deceased at the time of his death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(3A) the damages payable to the former wife are damages the subsection allows` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the dependant is a former wife of the deceased` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the damages payable to a former wife of the deceased"
        IF `the damages are in respect of a subsisting maintenance order against the deceased at the time of his death` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the damages payable to a former wife of the deceased shall only be in respect of a subsisting maintenance order against the deceased at the time of his death"

-- src:1471 | (4) If the dependants have incurred funeral expenses in respect of
-- src:1472 | the deceased, damages may be awarded in respect of those expenses.
@ref s 22(4) (src:1471-1472)
GIVEN `the dependants have incurred funeral expenses in respect of the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(4) damages may be awarded in respect of the funeral expenses` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the dependants have incurred funeral expenses in respect of the deceased` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the dependants have incurred funeral expenses in respect of the deceased, damages may be awarded in respect of those expenses" -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "if" is the text's no

-- src:1474 | (5) Money paid into court in satisfaction of a cause of action under
-- src:1475 | this Act may be in one sum without specifying any person’s share.
@ref s 22(5) (src:1474-1475)
GIVEN `the money is paid into court in satisfaction of a cause of action under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(5) the money may be paid in one sum without specifying any person's share` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the money is paid into court in satisfaction of a cause of action under this Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Money paid into court in satisfaction of a cause of action under this Act"

§§ `Sections 20 to 22 -- tests`

-- The helpers: calendar months, the leap-day roll, and the Interpretation Act's s 50(b)
#ASSERT `the same day of the month n months later` (Date 15 7 2025) 6 EQUALS Date 15 1 2026 -- an ordinary day
#ASSERT `the same day of the month n months later` (Date 31 8 2025) 6 EQUALS Date 28 2 2026 -- a shorter month: the last day of it
#ASSERT `the same day of the month n months later` (Date 29 2 2024) 36 EQUALS Date 28 2 2027 -- a leap day three years on, in a year that is not leap
#ASSERT `the same day of the month n months later` (Date 29 2 2024) 48 EQUALS Date 29 2 2028 -- four years on, a leap year
#ASSERT `the last day of the period of n months after` (Date 15 7 2025) 6 Months EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 2026) -- 15 January 2026 is a Thursday
#ASSERT `the last day of the period of n months after` (Date 15 11 2025) 6 Months EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 15 5 2026) -- 15 May 2026 is a Friday
#ASSERT `the last day of the period of n months after` (Date 2 11 2025) 6 Months EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 2 5 2026) -- 2 May 2026 is a Saturday, which the Interpretation Act s 50(b) does not move
#ASSERT `the last day of the period of n months after` (Date 3 11 2025) 6 Months EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 4 5 2026) -- 3 May 2026 is a Sunday, so the period includes the next day, Monday 4 May 2026
-- s 20(1), (2)
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the person is liable to an action for damages notwithstanding the death of the person injured` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "shall be liable to an action for damages, notwithstanding the death"
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the person is liable to an action for damages notwithstanding the death of the person injured` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not the person who would have been liable
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the person is liable to an action for damages notwithstanding the death of the person injured` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- death not caused by a wrongful act: "If death is caused"
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the person is liable to an action for damages notwithstanding the death of the person injured` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the injured person could not have recovered
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the action is for the benefit of the dependants of the deceased` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "for the benefit of the dependants"
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the action is for the benefit of the dependants of the deceased` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- "Subject to section 21(2)"
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the action is for the benefit of the dependants of the deceased` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not an action under section 20
-- s 20(3), (4)
#ASSERT `s 20(3) the action is brought as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- brought by and in the name of the executor or administrator
#ASSERT `s 20(3) the action is brought as the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a bare "shall be brought" (QB); see (4)
#ASSERT `s 20(3) the action is brought as the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not an action under section 20
#ASSERT `s 20(4) the action may be brought by and in the name of the persons for whose benefit an executor or administrator could have brought it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a) no executor or administrator
#ASSERT `s 20(4) the action may be brought by and in the name of the persons for whose benefit an executor or administrator could have brought it` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (b) no action within 6 months
#ASSERT `s 20(4) the action may be brought by and in the name of the persons for whose benefit an executor or administrator could have brought it` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- an executor exists and sued in time: "If"
-- the 6 months: both sides of the end (death 15 July 2025, last day 15 January 2026, a Thursday)
#ASSERT `s 20(4)(b) no action was brought by an executor or administrator within 6 months after the death` (Date 15 7 2025) NOTHING EMPTY EQUALS TRUE -- no action at all
#ASSERT `s 20(4)(b) no action was brought by an executor or administrator within 6 months after the death` (Date 15 7 2025) (JUST (Date 15 1 2026)) EMPTY EQUALS FALSE -- brought on the last day
#ASSERT `s 20(4)(b) no action was brought by an executor or administrator within 6 months after the death` (Date 15 7 2025) (JUST (Date 16 1 2026)) EMPTY EQUALS TRUE -- brought the day after the last day
#ASSERT `s 20(4)(b) no action was brought by an executor or administrator within 6 months after the death` (Date 15 7 2025) (JUST (Date 16 7 2025)) EMPTY EQUALS FALSE -- brought the day after the death
#ASSERT `s 20(4)(b) the first day after the 6 months` (Date 15 7 2025) EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 16 1 2026) -- the persons may bring the action from the day after the last day
-- s 20(5): both sides of the end (death 15 July 2025; last day 15 July 2028, a Saturday)
#ASSERT `s 20(5) the action is brought within 3 years after the death` (Date 15 7 2025) (Date 16 7 2025) EMPTY EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the day after the death
#ASSERT `s 20(5) the action is brought within 3 years after the death` (Date 15 7 2025) (Date 15 7 2025) EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the day of the death is not "after" it (fork F-P2)
#ASSERT `s 20(5) the action is brought within 3 years after the death` (Date 15 7 2025) (Date 15 7 2028) EMPTY EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the last day
#ASSERT `s 20(5) the action is brought within 3 years after the death` (Date 15 7 2025) (Date 16 7 2028) EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the day after the last day: "within 3 years"
#ASSERT `s 20(5) the action is brought within 3 years after the death` (Date 29 2 2024) (Date 1 3 2027) EMPTY EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a leap-day death: 28 February 2027 is a Sunday, so the last day is Monday 1 March 2027
#ASSERT `s 20(5) the action is brought within 3 years after the death` (Date 29 2 2024) (Date 2 3 2027) EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the day after that last day
#ASSERT `s 20(5) the number of days from the death to the last day for bringing the action` (Date 15 7 2025) EMPTY EQUALS JUST 1096 -- 15 July 2025 to 15 July 2028, counting the leap day
#ASSERT `s 20(5) a further action lies for the same subject matter of complaint` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "Not more than one action shall lie"
#ASSERT `s 20(5) a further action lies for the same subject matter of complaint` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- no earlier action: the subsection is silent
-- the regulative rules (a MAY that lapses ends FULFILLED, as does one that is used; the MUST in (6) stays outstanding until done)
#TRACE `s 20(3) and (5) the executor or administrator may bring the action within 3 years after the death` 1096 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `The executor or administrator of the deceased` DOES `bring the action by and in the name of the executor or administrator` AT 200
#TRACE `s 20(3) and (5) the executor or administrator may bring the action within 3 years after the death` 1096 AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 1100
#TRACE `s 20(4) the persons for whose benefit the action could have been brought may bring it within 3 years after the death` TRUE 1096 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `A person for whose benefit the action could have been brought` DOES `bring the action by and in the name of the persons for whose benefit it could have been brought` AT 200
#TRACE `s 20(4) the persons for whose benefit the action could have been brought may bring it within 3 years after the death` FALSE 1096 AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 10
-- s 20(6)
#ASSERT `s 20(6) the claimant is required to deliver full particulars to the defendant or his solicitor` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "shall be required to deliver"
#ASSERT `s 20(6) the claimant is required to deliver full particulars to the defendant or his solicitor` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not an action under section 20
#TRACE `s 20(6) the claimant must deliver full particulars to the defendant or his solicitor` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `The claimant in an action under section 20` DOES `deliver full particulars to the defendant or his solicitor` AT 5
#TRACE `s 20(6) the claimant must deliver full particulars to the defendant or his solicitor` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 400
#TRACE `s 20(6) the claimant must deliver full particulars to the defendant or his solicitor` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 400
-- s 20(7)
#ASSERT `s 20(7) the executor may insert a claim for and recover the pecuniary loss to the estate` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "may insert a claim for and recover"
#ASSERT `s 20(7) the executor may insert a claim for and recover the pecuniary loss to the estate` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not pecuniary loss to the estate
#ASSERT `s 20(7) the sum is deemed part of the assets of the estate of the deceased` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "shall be deemed part of the assets of the estate"
#ASSERT `s 20(7) the sum is deemed part of the assets of the estate of the deceased` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- another sum
-- s 20(8) to (11)
#ASSERT `s 20(8) the person is a dependant of the deceased` `The wife or husband of the deceased` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 20(8) the person is a dependant of the deceased` `The former wife of the deceased` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a), "former wife"
#ASSERT `s 20(8) the person is a dependant of the deceased` `A parent grandparent or great-grandparent of the deceased` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 20(8) the person is a dependant of the deceased` `A child grandchild or great-grandchild of the deceased` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (c)
#ASSERT `s 20(8) the person is a dependant of the deceased` `A person not a child of the deceased treated by the deceased as a child of the family in a marriage to which the deceased was a party` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (d)
#ASSERT `s 20(8) the person is a dependant of the deceased` `A person who is a brother sister uncle or aunt of the deceased` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (e), "is"
#ASSERT `s 20(8) the person is a dependant of the deceased` `A person who is the issue of a brother sister uncle or aunt of the deceased` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (e), "is the issue of"
#ASSERT `s 20(8) the person is a dependant of the deceased` `Another relationship` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "means"
#ASSERT `s 20(9)(a) the adopted person is treated as the child of the person` `By adoption by the person concerned` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the child of the person by whom he was adopted
#ASSERT `s 20(9)(a) the adopted person is treated as the child of the person` `By adoption into the family of someone else` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "and not as the child of any other person"
#ASSERT `s 20(9)(a) the adopted person is treated as the child of the person` `By blood` EQUALS NOTHING -- not an adopted person
#ASSERT `s 20(9)(b) the relationship is treated as the corresponding relationship by consanguinity or whole blood or child or legitimate child` `By affinity` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "any relationship by affinity shall be treated as a relationship by consanguinity"
#ASSERT `s 20(9)(b) the relationship is treated as the corresponding relationship by consanguinity or whole blood or child or legitimate child` `Of the half blood` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "of the half blood as a relationship of the whole blood"
#ASSERT `s 20(9)(b) the relationship is treated as the corresponding relationship by consanguinity or whole blood or child or legitimate child` `As a stepchild` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "the stepchild of any person as his child"
#ASSERT `s 20(9)(b) the relationship is treated as the corresponding relationship by consanguinity or whole blood or child or legitimate child` `As an illegitimate child of its mother or reputed father` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "an illegitimate person shall be treated as the legitimate child of his mother and reputed father"
#ASSERT `s 20(9)(b) the relationship is treated as the corresponding relationship by consanguinity or whole blood or child or legitimate child` `By adoption into the family of someone else` EQUALS NOTHING -- "subject to paragraph (a)"
#ASSERT `s 20(9)(b) the relationship is treated as the corresponding relationship by consanguinity or whole blood or child or legitimate child` `By blood` EQUALS NOTHING -- the paragraph names four bases
#ASSERT `s 20(8) with (9) the person is a dependant of the deceased` `A child grandchild or great-grandchild of the deceased` `By blood` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a child by blood
#ASSERT `s 20(8) with (9) the person is a dependant of the deceased` `A child grandchild or great-grandchild of the deceased` `As a stepchild` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a stepchild counts as a child
#ASSERT `s 20(8) with (9) the person is a dependant of the deceased` `A child grandchild or great-grandchild of the deceased` `By adoption into the family of someone else` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- adopted into another family (fork F-D2)
#ASSERT `s 20(8) with (9) the person is a dependant of the deceased` `Another relationship` `By blood` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not in the list
#ASSERT `s 20(10) the person is adopted for the purposes of subsection (9)(a)` `Adoption order under the Adoption of Children Act 2022` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "an adoption order made under the Adoption of Children Act 2022"
#ASSERT `s 20(10) the person is adopted for the purposes of subsection (9)(a)` `Adoption order under a corresponding previous written law` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "any corresponding previous written law"
#ASSERT `s 20(10) the person is adopted for the purposes of subsection (9)(a)` `Adoption recognised as valid by the law of Singapore` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "any adoption recognised as valid by the law of Singapore"
#ASSERT `s 20(10) the person is adopted for the purposes of subsection (9)(a)` `Another kind of adoption` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "means"
#ASSERT `s 20(11) the thing is injury` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a disease
#ASSERT `s 20(11) the thing is injury` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- an impairment of a person's physical or mental condition
#ASSERT `s 20(11) the thing is injury` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- "includes" does not close the list
-- s 21
#ASSERT `s 21(1) the action may consist of or include a claim for damages for bereavement` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "may consist of or include"
#ASSERT `s 21(1) the action may consist of or include a claim for damages for bereavement` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not an action under section 20
-- the cascade of s 21(2): flags are spouse, child, parent, treated-as-child, minor
#ASSERT `s 21(2) the claim for damages for bereavement is for the benefit of the person` `Surviving wife or husband of the deceased` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 21(2) the claim for damages for bereavement is for the benefit of the person` `Surviving child of the deceased` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (b), no spouse
#ASSERT `s 21(2) the claim for damages for bereavement is for the benefit of the person` `Surviving child of the deceased` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (b), a spouse can claim: "where there is no spouse"
#ASSERT `s 21(2) the claim for damages for bereavement is for the benefit of the person` `Surviving parent of the deceased or mother if the deceased was illegitimate` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (c)
#ASSERT `s 21(2) the claim for damages for bereavement is for the benefit of the person` `Surviving parent of the deceased or mother if the deceased was illegitimate` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (c), a child can claim
#ASSERT `s 21(2) the claim for damages for bereavement is for the benefit of the person` `Person who during a marriage treated the deceased minor as a child of the family` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (d), a minor deceased and nobody above
#ASSERT `s 21(2) the claim for damages for bereavement is for the benefit of the person` `Person who during a marriage treated the deceased minor as a child of the family` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (d), the deceased was not a minor
#ASSERT `s 21(2) the claim for damages for bereavement is for the benefit of the person` `Person who during a marriage treated the deceased minor as a child of the family` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (d), a parent can claim
#ASSERT `s 21(2) the claim for damages for bereavement is for the benefit of the person` `Surviving brother or sister of the deceased` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (e), nobody else
#ASSERT `s 21(2) the claim for damages for bereavement is for the benefit of the person` `Surviving brother or sister of the deceased` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (e), another person can claim
#ASSERT `s 21(2) the claim for damages for bereavement is for the benefit of the person` `Not in any of these classes` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "shall only be for the benefit of"
#ASSERT `s 21(2) the claim for damages for bereavement is for the benefit of the person` `Surviving wife or husband of the deceased` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- does not survive the deceased
#ASSERT `s 21(3) the right to claim survives for the benefit of the estate of the person` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "shall not survive for the benefit of his estate"
#ASSERT `s 21(3) the right to claim survives for the benefit of the estate of the person` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not the right under section 21
#ASSERT `s 21(4) the sum to be awarded as damages for bereavement` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST 15000 -- "shall be $15,000"
#ASSERT `s 21(4) the sum to be awarded as damages for bereavement` TRUE (JUST 20000) EQUALS JUST 20000 -- "Subject to subsection (6)": the Minister's order
#ASSERT `s 21(4) the sum to be awarded as damages for bereavement` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING -- not damages awarded under section 21
#ASSERT `s 21(5) the sum awarded is divided equally between the persons` 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 2 persons
#ASSERT `s 21(5) the sum awarded is divided equally between the persons` 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE -- one person: "2 or more"
#ASSERT `s 21(5) the share of each person` 15000 2 0 EQUALS JUST 7500 -- $15,000 between 2
#ASSERT `s 21(5) the share of each person` 15000 3 1500 EQUALS JUST 4500 -- $15,000 less $1,500 costs, between 3
#ASSERT `s 21(5) the share of each person` 15000 1 0 EQUALS NOTHING -- one person: the equal division is not stated
#ASSERT `s 21(6) the Minister has substituted the sum specified in subsection (4)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "by order published in the Gazette"
#ASSERT `s 21(6) the Minister has substituted the sum specified in subsection (4)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- no order among the sources
-- s 22
#ASSERT `s 22(1) the court may award damages proportioned to the losses resulting from the death to the dependants respectively` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "may award such damages"
#ASSERT `s 22(1) the court may award damages proportioned to the losses resulting from the death to the dependants respectively` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not an action under section 20
#ASSERT `s 22(1) the item is taken into account in assessing the damages` TRUE `A sum paid or payable under a contract of assurance or insurance` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 22(1) the item is taken into account in assessing the damages` TRUE `A sum payable under the Central Provident Fund Act 1953` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 22(1) the item is taken into account in assessing the damages` TRUE `A pension or gratuity paid or payable as a result of the death` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (c)
#ASSERT `s 22(1) the item is taken into account in assessing the damages` TRUE `Another item` EQUALS NOTHING -- not named
#ASSERT `s 22(1) the item is taken into account in assessing the damages` FALSE `A sum payable under the Central Provident Fund Act 1953` EQUALS NOTHING -- not an action under section 20
#ASSERT `s 22(1A) the court takes the benefit into account in assessing the damages` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "shall take into account"
#ASSERT `s 22(1A) the court takes the benefit into account in assessing the damages` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- succession
#ASSERT `s 22(1A) the court takes the benefit into account in assessing the damages` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- another benefit
#ASSERT `s 22(2) costs not recovered are deducted and the damages are divided among the dependants` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "shall be deducted ... and ... divided"
#ASSERT `s 22(2) costs not recovered are deducted and the damages are divided among the dependants` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no damages awarded under (1): "Where"
#ASSERT `s 22(2) the share of the dependant` TRUE 100000 10000 0.5 EQUALS JUST 45000 -- (100000 less 10000 costs) half
#ASSERT `s 22(2) the share of the dependant` FALSE 100000 10000 0.5 EQUALS NOTHING -- no damages awarded under (1)
#ASSERT `s 22(3) the remarriage of the widow or her prospect of remarriage is taken into account` TRUE `The remarriage or prospect of remarriage of a widow` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "shall not be taken into account"
#ASSERT `s 22(3) the remarriage of the widow or her prospect of remarriage is taken into account` TRUE `Another item` EQUALS NOTHING -- not the remarriage
#ASSERT `s 22(3) the remarriage of the widow or her prospect of remarriage is taken into account` FALSE `The remarriage or prospect of remarriage of a widow` EQUALS NOTHING -- not damages payable to a widow
#ASSERT `s 22(3A) the damages payable to the former wife are damages the subsection allows` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "in respect of a subsisting maintenance order"
#ASSERT `s 22(3A) the damages payable to the former wife are damages the subsection allows` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "shall only be in respect of"
#ASSERT `s 22(3A) the damages payable to the former wife are damages the subsection allows` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a former wife
#ASSERT `s 22(4) damages may be awarded in respect of the funeral expenses` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "damages may be awarded in respect of those expenses"
#ASSERT `s 22(4) damages may be awarded in respect of the funeral expenses` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no funeral expenses incurred: "If"
#ASSERT `s 22(5) the money may be paid in one sum without specifying any person's share` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "may be in one sum"
#ASSERT `s 22(5) the money may be paid in one sum without specifying any person's share` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- money not paid in under this Act
